.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt SCHED_ULE 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sched_ule
.Nd ULE scheduler
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "options SCHED_ULE"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
scheduler
provides a number of advanced scheduler
features not present in
.Xr sched_4bsd 4 ,
the traditional system scheduler.
These features address SMP and interactivity and include:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact -offset indent
.It
Thread CPU affinity.
.It
CPU topology awareness, including for hyper-threading.
.It
Per-CPU run queues.
.It
Interactivity heuristics that detect interactive applications and schedules
them preferentially under high load.
.El
.Pp
Common scheduler sysctls are documented in
.Xr scheduler 4 .
.Pp
The following sysctls are relevant to the operation of
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va kern.sched.ule.quantum
The length of the timeshare quantum in microseconds.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.slice
The length of the timeshare quantum in statclock ticks.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.interact
The interactivity score threshold.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.preempt_thresh
The non-inclusive numerical priority threshold below which preemption is allowed.
Threads with numerically-lower priority values have higher priority.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.static_boost
The minimum priority (maximum numerical value) to be applied to a thread on wakeup.
Value 1 indicates to use a priority specified statically by the kernel at the point of sleep.
Value 0 indicates to keep the current thread's priority at wakeup.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.idlespins
The number of times an idle thread spins while waiting for work.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.idlespinthresh
The context switch threshold for idle thread spinning.
.El
.Pp
The following sysctls are available only on SMP systems:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va kern.sched.ule.affinity
The number of clock ticks for which a thread retains CPU affinity.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.balance
Whether to enable the long-term load balancer.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.balance_interval
The average interval, in statclock ticks, between long-term load balancing
passes.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.steal_thresh
The minimum load on a remote CPU before attempting to steal work.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.always_steal
Whether the idle thread always tries to steal work.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.steal_idle
Whether to try stealing work from another CPU before idling.
.It Va kern.sched.ule.trysteal_limit
The topological distance limit for stealing threads during a context switch.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr scheduler 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
scheduler first appeared in
.Fx 5.1 .
